ationships (20320, 20284)]\n\n## International influence on Madrid's healthcare practices\n\nMadrid's healthcare practices are influenced by international standards and guidelines, particularly from organizations like the World Health Organization. The city's healthcare system incorporates these global standards to enhance the quality of care provided to patients, including those in vulnerable situations such as hunger strikes. This international perspective enriches the local healthcare practices and ensures they are aligned with best practices worldwide. [Data: Entities (50, 15908); Relationships (5182, 20330)]\"\r\n337,\"# Endocrinology and Nutrition Community in Asturias\n\nThe community is centered around key medical professionals and institutions specializing in endocrinology and nutrition in Asturias, Spain. The entities are interconnected through their roles in healthcare, research, and education, particularly in managing diabetes and providing nutritional support for various medical conditions.\n\n## Key medical professionals in endocrinology and nutrition\n\nThe community includes several prominent medical professionals such as Dr. Francisco Villazón González, Dra. Nuria Valdés Gallego, and Dr. Paula Fernández Martínez, who are recognized for their contributions to endocrinology and nutrition. Dr. Villazón González is particularly noted for his work on diabetes mellitus in Spain, which highlights the community's focus on managing chronic health conditions. His affiliation with the Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias further emphasizes the importance of this institution in providing specialized care. [Data: Entities (6511, 3661, 12671); Relationships (1534)]\n\n## Significant healthcare institutions\n\nThe Hospital Universitario Central de Asturias and the Complejo Asistencial Universitario are vital healthcare institutions in this community. They provide comprehensive medical services, particularly in endocrinology and nutrition, and are home to man